               <children>
                  <Text fx:id="GenText" fill="WHITE" layoutY="22.740234375" strokeType="OUTSIDE" strokeWidth="0.0" style="-fx-font-color: #000000;" text="Welcome to the General Help section of our Product Management System! Here, you'll find essential information to help you get started and make the most out of our application:The Security Module implements multi-level system access to protect sensitive data, featuring admin, kitchen staff, and cashier user accounts with tailored access controls. Security measures include OTP verification, password recovery via security questions, and user activity monitoring. The Account Manager Module manages user accounts, including creation, modification, and deactivation, handling user registration and ensuring administrative privilege access.The Order Module facilitates order creation and retrieval, applies discount for PWD and senior citizens, and tracks stock levels needed for fulfilling orders, supporting in-person and online order management while adjusting stock quantities accordingly.The Sales/Transactions Management Module oversees sales operations, including transaction creation, history viewing, and payment recording, calculating discounts and updating inventory upon transaction completion. The inventory Module manages inventory for raw materials and finished products, tracking stock levels, restocks, and expiration dates. It uses a forecasting algorithm to handle recommended reorder points and handle inventory adjustments for various stock items.The Report Generation Module generates and analyzes sales reports, providing insights into sales performance, product popularity, and financial metrics, with reports viewable digitally, esportable as PDFs, or emailable to user.The Email Messenger Module sends system-generated emails, such as reports and OTP codes, ensuring users receive relevant information. The Search Module allows users to search the relational database efficiently, integrated into various modules to locate specific information using keywords and filters. " textAlignment="JUSTIFY" wrappingWidth="1017.8034210205078" AnchorPane.bottomAnchor="-218.0" AnchorPane.leftAnchor="0.0" AnchorPane.rightAnchor="-100.0" AnchorPane.topAnchor="-1.0">
